SPIRV-Tools: optimizer passes from flags, ending in an error, never the process

What: pingouinOptimizeWithFlags(env, flags, count, max_id_bound, binary, words, &out)
runs the spirv-opt passes the flags name over a binary, without the validator
before them (the caller validated it) and with the id bound capped, and returns
SPV_SUCCESS and the result (spvBinaryDestroy), SPV_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE for an
unknown flag, or SPV_ERROR_INTERNAL when a pass fails (an id past the bound) or a
C++ exception is thrown. Every step that allocates (the optimizer, its passes,
the options, the result) is inside one try/catch; diagnostics are dropped.
Why: Venus inlines the calls of guest modules whose functions take an array by
value before MoltenVK reads them (virgl-venus-spirv-inline-array-calls.patch),
on the thread of the guest's command ring. spvOptimizerRun alone is not enough:
spvOptimizerCreate and the pass registration allocate outside it, and its own
`new` checks never see a NULL (new throws). The library is built with
exceptions and with assert() that throws (spirv-tools-val-catch-throws.patch
applies to SPIRV-Tools-opt as well), so a failed assert or std::bad_alloc in a
pass would else end QEMU.
Upstream: no (a Pingouin entry point).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-spirv-validate.sh (the inline unit: every corpus
module with an array parameter is inlined, valid, with none left; an unknown flag
is SPV_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE; an id bound below the module's is an error, not the
end of the process).

diff --git a/include/spirv-tools/libspirv.h b/include/spirv-tools/libspirv.h
--- a/include/spirv-tools/libspirv.h
+++ b/include/spirv-tools/libspirv.h
@@ -1089,6 +1089,18 @@ SPIRV_TOOLS_EXPORT spv_result_t spvOptimizerRun(
     spv_optimizer_t* optimizer, const uint32_t* binary, const size_t word_count,
     spv_binary* optimized_binary, const spv_optimizer_options options);
 
+// Pingouin: the passes named by `flags` (spirv-opt's, e.g. "--merge-return")
+// over `binary`, without the validator before them and with the id bound capped
+// at `max_id_bound`, all inside try/catch: SPV_SUCCESS and the result in
+// *optimized_binary (free it with spvBinaryDestroy), or an error and NULL. An
+// unknown flag is SPV_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE; a pass that fails (an id past the
+// bound) or a C++ exception (a failed assert(), which throws in this build,
+// std::bad_alloc) is SPV_ERROR_INTERNAL instead of the end of the process.
+SPIRV_TOOLS_EXPORT spv_result_t pingouinOptimizeWithFlags(
+    spv_target_env env, const char* const* flags, size_t flag_count,
+    uint32_t max_id_bound, const uint32_t* binary, size_t word_count,
+    spv_binary* optimized_binary);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
diff --git a/source/opt/optimizer.cpp b/source/opt/optimizer.cpp
--- a/source/opt/optimizer.cpp
+++ b/source/opt/optimizer.cpp
@@ -1316,4 +1316,44 @@ spv_result_t spvOptimizerRun(spv_optimizer_t* optimizer,
   return SPV_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+// Pingouin (spirv-tools-opt-catch-throws.patch): Venus runs passes on guest
+// SPIR-V on the thread of a guest's command ring; an exception there must end
+// the call, not QEMU. Every step that allocates is inside the try.
+spv_result_t pingouinOptimizeWithFlags(spv_target_env env,
+                                       const char* const* flags,
+                                       size_t flag_count, uint32_t max_id_bound,
+                                       const uint32_t* binary,
+                                       size_t word_count,
+                                       spv_binary* optimized_binary) {
+  *optimized_binary = nullptr;
+  try {
+    spvtools::Optimizer optimizer(env);
+    // no message consumer: diagnostics are dropped, the result says it all
+    optimizer.SetMessageConsumer(
+        [](spv_message_level_t, const char*, const spv_position_t&,
+           const char*) {});
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < flag_count; i++) {
+      if (!optimizer.RegisterPassFromFlag(flags[i]))
+        return SPV_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE;
+    }
+    std::unique_ptr<spv_optimizer_options_t,
+                    decltype(&spvOptimizerOptionsDestroy)>
+        options(spvOptimizerOptionsCreate(), spvOptimizerOptionsDestroy);
+    spvOptimizerOptionsSetRunValidator(options.get(), false);
+    spvOptimizerOptionsSetMaxIdBound(options.get(), max_id_bound);
+    std::vector<uint32_t> optimized;
+    if (!optimizer.Run(binary, word_count, &optimized, options.get()))
+      return SPV_ERROR_INTERNAL;
+    auto result = std::make_unique<spv_binary_t>();
+    auto code = std::make_unique<uint32_t[]>(optimized.size());
+    memcpy(code.get(), optimized.data(), optimized.size() * sizeof(uint32_t));
+    result->code = code.release();
+    result->wordCount = optimized.size();
+    *optimized_binary = result.release();
+    return SPV_SUCCESS;
+  } catch (...) {
+    return SPV_ERROR_INTERNAL;
+  }
+}
+
 }  // extern "C"
